---
// The Nov 2026 member-driven press release, shown as a modal on /media.
// It has no page of its own: the shareable link is /media#<PRESS_RELEASE_ID>,
// which opens the dialog on load (see the script below). Keep the id in sync
// with the press release entry in src/pages/media.astro.
const PRESS_RELEASE_ID = "member-driven-press-release";
---

<dialog
  id={PRESS_RELEASE_ID}
  class="m-auto max-h-[calc(100dvh-32px)] w-[min(760px,calc(100%-32px))] max-w-none overflow-y-auto overscroll-contain rounded-2xl border-0 bg-white p-0 text-gray-800 shadow-xl backdrop:bg-black/60"
  aria-labelledby="pr-title"
>
  <div
    class="sticky top-0 z-10 flex items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-gray-200 bg-white px-6 py-3"
  >
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-500">Press release</p>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <button
        type="button"
        data-pr-copy
        class="rounded-full border border-gray-300 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-gray-700 transition hover:bg-gray-50"
      >
        Copy link
      </button>
      <button
        type="button"
        data-pr-close
        aria-label="Close press release"
        class="grid h-9 w-9 place-items-center rounded-full text-gray-700 transition hover:bg-gray-100"
      >
        <svg
          width="20"
          height="20"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2.25"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path>
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="px-6 pb-8 pt-6 text-[15px] leading-relaxed sm:px-10">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE - November 2, 2026</p>

    <h2 id="pr-title" class="mt-4 text-2xl font-bold leading-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl">
      Tech for Palestine, Behind Apps With More Than 10 Million Users, Becomes a Member-Driven
      Organization
    </h2>

    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-gray-700">
      After three years as an incubator, Tech for Palestine is ready for more: more projects, built
      faster, with more impact. That is why it now puts members at the center.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4">
      Tech for Palestine (T4P), whose projects have reached more than 10 million users in less than
      three years, today opened its membership to the public. From November 2, anyone can become a
      member and build advocacy projects under the T4P banner. Members get a team to work with and
      the backing of the organization behind Big Tech alternatives such as UpScrolled and Thaura,
      and advocacy tools such as Boycat and NewsCord.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">
      From incubator to member-driven organization
    </h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      For the past three years, the T4P incubator helped the people behind more than 90 initiatives
      turn their ideas into advocacy tools. Those teams received mentorship, connections and
      support, but the building itself happened in their own organizations, outside T4P.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      T4P is now bringing the building inside. The support it offered external teams is available to
      every member. New projects carry the T4P name, and members build them together.
    </p>
    <blockquote class="mt-4 border-l-4 border-[#cd3b26] pl-4 italic text-gray-700">
      “Our incubator proved that small teams with the right skills can build tools used by millions.
      Now we build with many more people, and with far less distance between an idea and the team
      that ships it.”
    </blockquote>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">How membership works</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Members join with the skills they have: engineering, design, research, writing or organizing.
      Some join an existing project that needs their expertise. Others bring their own idea and
      start a new team, which T4P mentors help scope, staff with fellow members and take to a first
      public version.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      The model can move fast. When Macklemore was dropped from Ed Sheeran’s US tour after saying
      “Free Palestine” on stage, he explained that Sheeran could not get past his public stance of
      “I don’t take sides.” T4P members picked up the moment and built Ed Takes No Sides, a
      directory where artists who do take a stand for Palestine can create a profile and be found.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">
      25+ projects from a 200-member private beta
    </h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Before the public launch, T4P tested membership for several months with 200 members. In that
      time, members built more than 25 new advocacy projects, including:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-6">
      <li>Israel Bonds Tracker, a platform that raises awareness about Israeli bonds.</li>
      <li>
        Sponsored internships connecting students from Gaza with internships in the UK and Ireland.
      </li>
      <li>
        Profile Pic Maker, revived by members: a tool that adds a Palestinian-flag frame to social
        media profile pictures.
      </li>
      <li>
        A research team investigating bias against Palestinians in frontier large language models.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Two ways to join</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      <strong>Members</strong> contribute time and skills. They can join an existing team or form a new
      one with members who complement their skills. Sign-up is at
      <a href="/membership" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">techforpalestine.org/membership</a
      >, and the T4P team helps each new member find a first project.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      <strong>Supporting members</strong> back the work financially and leave the building to others.
      Their dues fund the marketing, engineering, mentorship, software access, partnerships and grants
      that T4P provides to its projects. Details are at
      <a href="/supporting-member" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline"
        >techforpalestine.org/supporting-member</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Media contact</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Afzal Mangal -
      <a href="mailto:afzal@techforpalestine.org" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline"
        >afzal@techforpalestine.org</a
      >
    </p>
  </article>
</dialog>

<style>
  :global(html:has(#member-driven-press-release[open])) {
    overflow: hidden;
  }
</style>

<script>
  const ID = "member-driven-press-release";
  const HASH = `#${ID}`;
  const dialog = document.getElementById(ID);

  if (dialog instanceof HTMLDialogElement && typeof dialog.showModal === "function") {
    const open = () => {
      if (dialog.open) return;
      dialog.showModal();
      window.plausible?.("Press Release Opened", { props: { id: ID } });
    };

    // Card links use href="#id": open the modal instead of jumping to it, and
    // keep the hash in the URL so the address bar holds the shareable link.
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>(`a[href="${HASH}"]`).forEach((link) => {
      link.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
        event.preventDefault();
        history.replaceState(null, "", HASH);
        open();
      });
    });

    dialog.querySelector("[data-pr-close]")?.addEventListener("click", () => dialog.close());
    // A click whose target is the <dialog> itself landed on the backdrop.
    dialog.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
      if (event.target === dialog) dialog.close();
    });
    dialog.addEventListener("close", () => {
      if (location.hash === HASH) {
        history.replaceState(null, "", location.pathname + location.search);
      }
    });

    const copyButton = dialog.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-pr-copy]");
    copyButton?.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const url = `${location.origin}${location.pathname}${HASH}`;
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(url);
        copyButton.textContent = "Link copied";
      } catch {
        copyButton.textContent = "Copy failed";
      }
      window.setTimeout(() => (copyButton.textContent = "Copy link"), 2000);
    });

    if (location.hash === HASH) open();
    window.addEventListener("hashchange", () => {
      if (location.hash === HASH) open();
    });
  }
</script>
